    "id": 3528354,
    "postDate": "2026-09-25T23:45:44.790Z",
    "rawMarkdown": "There is still 1 month remaining, so that gives lots of time to succeed even if you only use 1 GPU. Currently I am participating with one L40S 48GB GPU. I queue a sequence of experiments on a single L40S 48GB GPU. Each experiment takes a few hours, so we get dozens of experiments each day.\n\nIn about a week, my experiments have found some strong single models and a LB 0.945 ensemble (without using public notebook models)! (Note I am not using public notebook models. If we use public notebook models, the search is quicker because we just search for something to improve public notebooks and don't start from scratch).",
    "content": "<p>There is still 1 month remaining, so that gives lots of time to succeed even if you only use 1 GPU. Currently I am participating with one L40S 48GB GPU. I queue a sequence of experiments on a single L40S 48GB GPU. Each experiment takes a few hours, so we get dozens of experiments each day.</p>\n<p>In about a week, my experiments have found some strong single models and a LB 0.945 ensemble (without using public notebook models)! (Note I am not using public notebook models. If we use public notebook models, the search is quicker because we just search for something to improve public notebooks and don't start from scratch).</p>",
    "parent": {},
