        "id": 3528321,
        "postDate": "2026-09-25T21:07:48.350Z",
        "rawMarkdown": "You can do that if you want or you can create the dataset directly in the Kaggle notebook, again using the Kaggle APIs. Same outcome, first skips the commit + download step, it just uploads directly from the notebook when you run it. Ask a LLM, it'll know what to do but you certainly should not be reading any DICOMs from a Google Drive folder. ",
        "content": "<p>You can do that if you want or you can create the dataset directly in the Kaggle notebook, again using the Kaggle APIs. Same outcome, first skips the commit + download step, it just uploads directly from the notebook when you run it. Ask a LLM, it'll know what to do but you certainly should not be reading any DICOMs from a Google Drive folder. </p>",
